/T (Karachi's small property market has experienced a dynamic trajectory over the past decade. Following strong growth in 2012-2014, culminating in a staggering 106% increase in 2014, the market faced a period of stagnation and even minor declines from 2016-2018. However, a resurgence began in 2019, with steady growth culminating in 13% increases in both 2022 and 2023. This volatility resulted in an overall cumulative return of 187% over the ten-year period vs 195% cumulative return by all small properties in Pakistan. highlighting the surge in demand for small houses. The recent three-year cumulative return of 31% suggests a renewed period of growth and a hedge against inflationary pressure.)
